avorite favorite favorite way to do it  is to try to start on a really small  project and then over  like crazy so try to find you know you  may have an ideal client that you're  going after and it may be worth a lot of  money to you try to start on a really  small project with them and that project  you may not make a lot of money on I  wouldn't cut my my pricing down too much  but I would spend a lot of time and  effort on the service and the delivery  of whatever product you're producing you  basically want to take one small project  that's really low risk for them so you  can say just try me out we do a really  small order let me prove myself to you  let me show you how we can really wow  you right everybody else and you know  because it's a little risk to them  they're more likely to say yes then you  come in you go crazy on this first order  you know make sure they love you try to  add a couple of other things on the  service side too really wild and  compared to what your competition is  doing and then when it's time to reorder  who are they gonna go with and your your  the company who's really stood out so  they're gonna want to keep coming back  in ordering from you and this is  strategy I use over and over and over  again with my clients I get hired by  corporate clients who asked me to create  content for their websites for example  and they may hire me as well as 50 other  bloggers who are trying to create  content as well and what I do is always  try to go above and beyond the  expectation so you know they ask you 500  words I'll usually create at least a  thousand or 1500 words a lot of video on  top of it I'll then promote it and  market it and show you know my readers  what I'm doing and drive traffic to them  and promote them and give them a lot of  exposure so that my articles end up  getting you know ten times plus the  amount of traffic and comments and with  everybody else  so then when it's time to you know  negotiate an extension they're gonna